(Determined on the basis of the major time criterion over a 365-day reference period. Categories:) Tj
T* (- Workers \(self-employed: own account, employer, contributing family worker; salaried/regular; casual wage\)) Tj
T* (- Unemployed \(seeking and available\)) Tj
T* (- Out of labour force \(students, domestic duties, pensioners, disabled\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
54. 706.8899999999999864 Td
(2.3 Employment Status Categories) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 691.8899999999999864 Td
(**Self-employed**: Own-account workers \(work alone\), Employers \(hire others\), Contributing family workers \(unpaid) Tj
T* (work in family enterprise\).) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (**Regular/Salaried employees**: Work for others on a regular basis and receive salary/wage.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (**Casual wage labourers**: Work on a day-to-day or casual basis; do not have regular/long-term work contract.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
54. 603.8899999999999864 Td
(2.4 Formal vs. Informal Employment) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 588.8899999999999864 Td
(Informal employment encompasses all jobs lacking basic social or legal protections or employment benefits-whether) Tj
T* (in formal or informal sector enterprises. Estimated using PLFS variables on job contract type, social security) Tj
T* (coverage, and written job contract. India has a very high share \(~90%\) of informal employment.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 13 Tf
14.9499999999999993 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
48. 527.8899999999999864 Td
(3. Estimation Methodology) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
54. 509.8899999999999864 Td
(3.1 Step 1: Weight Assignment) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 494.8899999999999864 Td
(Each sampled household is assigned a design weight = inverse of the probability of selection. Weights are calibrated) Tj
T* (to known population totals \(from Census/population projections\) by state, sector \(rural/urban\), age group, and sex.) Tj
T* (This corrects for differential non-response and improves precision.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
54. 445.8899999999999864 Td
(3.2 Step 2: Activity Classification) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 430.8899999999999864 Td
(Each person 15+ years is classified into activity status categories \(worker/unemployed/OOLF\) based on:) Tj
T* (- Usual Principal Activity \(UPA\): Major time in 365 days) Tj
T* (- Usual Subsidiary Activity \(USA\): Minor time in 365 days) Tj
T* (- Current Weekly Status \(CWS\): Activity in past 7 days) Tj
T* (- Current Daily Status \(CDS\): Activity each day of reference week) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
54. 355.8899999999999864 Td
(3.3 Step 3: Indicator Computation) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 340.8899999999999864 Td
(Weighted estimates of employed, unemployed, and labour force are computed by summing person-weights across) Tj
T* (relevant categories:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (␀E␀s␀t␀i␀m␀a␀t␀e␀d␀ ␀E␀m␀p␀l␀o␀y␀e␀d␀ ␀=␀ £␀ ␀\(␀w␀e␀i␀g␀h␀t␀_␀i␀ ␀×␀ ␀e␀m␀p␀l␀o␀y␀e␀d␀_␀i␀n␀d␀i␀c␀a␀t␀o␀r␀_␀i␀\)) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (LFPR = \(Estimated Labour Force / Estimated Population 15+\) × 100) Tj
T* (WPR = \(Estimated Employed / Estimated Population 15+\) × 100) Tj
T* (UR = \(Estimated Unemployed / Estimated Labour Force\) × 100) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
54. 226.8899999999999864 Td
(3.4 Step 4: Standard Error Estimation) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 211.8899999999999864 Td
(Given the complex multi-stage stratified design, standard errors cannot be computed using simple random sampling) Tj
T* (formulas. Methods used:) Tj
T* (- Taylor linearisation \(approximate variance estimation\)) Tj
T* (- Jackknife replication) Tj
T* (- Bootstrap methods) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Published estimates include standard errors and coefficients of variation \(CV\) to indicate reliability.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
54. 110.8899999999999864 Td
(3.5 Step 5: Disaggregation) Tj
