(**Pitfall 2 - Female LFPR in India**: India's female LFPR appears low by international standards but household work) Tj
T* (and subsistence activity are excluded. Using UPSS \(principal + subsidiary\) gives higher female WPR than UPS alone.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
48. 322.8899999999999864 Td
(␀*␀*␀P␀i␀t␀f␀a␀l␀l␀ ␀3␀ ␀-␀ ␀L␀o␀w␀ ␀u␀n␀e␀m␀p␀l␀o␀y␀m␀e␀n␀t␀ "`␀ ␀f␀u␀l␀l␀ ␀e␀m␀p␀l␀o␀y␀m␀e␀n␀t␀*␀*␀:␀ ␀I␀n␀ ␀t␀h␀e␀ ␀a␀b␀s␀e␀n␀c␀e␀ ␀o␀f␀ ␀s␀o␀c␀i␀a␀l␀ ␀p␀r␀o␀t␀e␀c␀t␀i␀o␀n␀,␀ ␀p␀e␀o␀p␀l␀e␀ ␀c␀a␀n␀n␀o␀t␀ ␀a␀f␀f␀o␀r␀d␀ ␀t␀o␀ ␀b␀e) Tj
T* (unemployed; they accept low-quality, low-wage casual work. This is reflected in high CDS unemployment \(capturing) Tj
T* (underemployment\).) Tj
